A||||13||AL||keyhole for drivers side don't work||||1||
Z||000000||AL||01-11-2000||08:27 PM||||ok guys my drivers side keyhole is busted, now i can't get my key in, do i have to go to the dealer so they can put in a nw one that will accept my old key or what?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-12-2000||12:14 AM||||The dealer will send you to a locksmith who will charge you big bucks to get the old cylinder out. If you can get it out yourself then the locksmith can set it up quick and easy to fit your existing key.  Might have to buy a new blank cylinder from the dealer tho.  Maybe somebody knows an easy way to get a door cylinder out??||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||01-12-2000||12:16 AM||||They come out from the inside. Take the panel off then the clip that holds the lock||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-12-2000||03:59 AM||||Inner door panel off, rod off of lock cylinder (sm. clip holds it on), remove U shaped clip holding lock cylinder on (slides to the front-don't drop it), pull lock cylinder out from/to the inside.  Piece of cake unless the U shaped clip is bent like mine was.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||01-11-2000||11:10 PM||||I KNOW HOW TO TAKE IT OUT, BUT MY QUESTION IS CAN I GET ANOTHER CYLNDER TO EXCEPT MY KEY WITHOUT REPLACIG BOTH. DO I HAVE TO GO TO THE DEALER OR WHAT, I DON'T WANT TO CARRY TOO SETS OF KEYS TO OPEN THE DOORS.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sage||01-12-2000||09:37 AM||||Chill...and check Phaetons reply.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||01-12-2000||09:57 AM||||If you take either a) your existing door key or b) your VIN and proof of ownership to your local dealer, they can sell you a new door lock cylinder to fit your existing key.<P>Now, as far as installation goes, I thought it was a major pain in the a$$.  I had to have a friend with small hands finish the job.||||reg||1
