Z||000012||bHooper||01-13-2000||08:37 PM||||Al, when i first got my car... far, far ago, i had a similar problem with the rear lock as well as a door lock.  it was dificult to get the key in.  the locksmith fixed it quick and cheap!  apparently the "doors" that slide closed to protect the actuall mechanism are plastic and come loose or break!  so you might want to check that.<P>brian||||reg||4
Z||000013||Monkeyman||01-14-2000||04:11 AM||||Sage-I've got meds for anything that ails ya.  I <B> do </B> tend to play my music loud but only if it's crystal clear.  I don't care for the kids who want alot of bass just to vibrate the windows.  It has to sound good or it has to be turned off.<P>Al-I recently got a hearing exam at work.  I'm not deaf, but apparently I have a (very) mild case of hearing loss.  The only time it bothers me is when there's more than one thing going on at a time.  If the TVs on and someone's trying to talk to me, I can't seem to hear either one 100%.  No big deal.  Just turn the music up louder!||||reg||1
